      "content": "1. Foundation of the Mughal Empire"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Mughal Empire was founded by Babur, who ruled from 1526 to 1530.",
        "Key rulers shaping the empire include Babur, Humayun, Akbar the Great, Jahangir, Shah Jahan, and Aurangzeb.",
        "Mughal Administration, along with Art and Architecture, formed the structural and cultural backbone of the empire.",
        "The gradual decline of the Mughal Empire marks a crucial transition period in Indian history frequently assessed in competitive exams."
